{"id":"CVE-2013-4545","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2013-11-23T11:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-06T16:45:14.830Z","description":"cURL and libcurl 7.18.0 through 7.32.0, when built with OpenSSL, disables the certificate CN and SAN name field verification (CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYHOST) when the digital signature verification (CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYPEER) is disabled, which allows man-in-the-middle attackers to spoof SSL servers via an arbitrary valid certificate.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.oracle.com/technetwork/topics/security/cpujul2015-2367936.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://h20564.www2.hp.com/hpsc/doc/public/display?docId=emr_na-c04463322","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_HP"],"name":"HPSBMU03112"},{"url":"http://curl.haxx.se/docs/adv_20131115.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.oracle.com/technetwork/topics/security/cpujan2015-1972971.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.oracle.com/technetwork/topics/security/cpuapr2015-2365600.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.debian.org/security/2013/dsa-2798","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_DEBIAN"],"name":"DSA-2798"},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-updates/2013-12/msg00047.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"openSUSE-SU-2013:1859"},{"url":"http://www.ubuntu.com/usn/USN-2048-1","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-2048-1"},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-updates/2013-12/msg00053.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"openSUSE-SU-2013:1865"}],"vendors":["curl","openssl"]}
{"id":"CVE-2013-6422","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2013-12-23T22:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-06T17:39:01.250Z","description":"The GnuTLS backend in libcurl 7.21.4 through 7.33.0, when disabling digital signature verification (CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYPEER), also disables the CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYHOST check for CN or SAN host name fields, which makes it easier for remote attackers to spoof servers and conduct man-in-the-middle (MITM) attacks.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://curl.haxx.se/docs/adv_20131217.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.oracle.com/technetwork/topics/security/cpujul2015-2367936.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://h20564.www2.hp.com/hpsc/doc/public/display?docId=emr_na-c04463322","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_HP"],"name":"HPSBMU03112"},{"url":"http://www.debian.org/security/2013/dsa-2824","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_DEBIAN"],"name":"DSA-2824"},{"url":"http://www.ubuntu.com/usn/USN-2058-1","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-2058-1"}],"vendors":["crypto-libs","curl"]}
